            "padding_top_desktop": "desktop:pt-xxl",
            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-xl",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<p>Waking up congested, sneezing through the night, or struggling to breathe during allergy season makes a home feel less like a sanctuary. Choosing the right air filter makes a measurable difference. With many options available, understanding what actually works helps you identify the best solution for your specific health needs.</p><h3><strong>Why Indoor Air Quality Matters</strong></h3><p>Most people spend about 90 percent of their time indoors, where<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/blogs/news/indoor-pollution\"> <span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">air can be up to five times more polluted than outdoor air</span></a>. Dust, pet dander, pollen, mold spores, and volatile organic compounds accumulate in enclosed spaces. For allergy and asthma sufferers, these invisible particles trigger symptoms that disrupt sleep, concentration, and daily comfort.</p><p>Quality air filtration actively removes these contaminants, creating a cleaner breathing environment. However, not all filtration systems perform equally. Understanding the differences between filtration technologies helps you identify the best choice for your individual health goals.</p><h3><strong>What Makes an Air Filter Effective</strong></h3>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "s3"
          }
        },
        "image_caption_QBGK76": {
          "type": "image_caption",
