            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-lg",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<p>When searching for the best air filter for allergies or asthma, focus on these key factors: particle capture rate (how small of particles can it trap), Clean Air Delivery Rate or CADR (how quickly does it purify the room), noise level (can it run at night without disruption), and energy efficiency (is it practical for continuous use).</p><p>Standard HEPA filters capture 99.97 percent of particles at 0.3 microns. While effective, newer technologies surpass these benchmarks. Blueair's proprietary<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/pages/blueair-performance\"> <span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">HEPASilent™ technology</span></a> combines mechanical filtration with electrostatic charging. As air passes through the purifier, particles receive an electrical charge that makes them adhere to filter fibers more effectively. The result captures 99.97 percent of airborne particles down to 0.1 microns.</p><p>To put that in perspective, pollen grains measure around 10 microns. HEPASilent™ technology captures particles 100 times smaller, including fine dust, bacteria, and smoke particles that standard filters might miss.</p><h3><strong>Best Air Filter for Homes with Allergies</strong></h3>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "p2"
          }
        },
        "image_caption_qy8nHW": {
          "type": "image_caption",
          "settings": {
            "margin_top_mobile": "mt-0",
            "margin_bottom_mobile": "mb-0",
