        "text_WK8EhA": {
          "type": "text",
          "settings": {
            "margin_top_mobile": "mt-md",
            "margin_bottom_mobile": "mb-md",
            "padding_top_mobile": "pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_mobile": "pb-lg",
            "margin_top_desktop": "desktop:mt-lg",
            "margin_bottom_desktop": "desktop:mb-lg",
            "padding_top_desktop": "desktop:pt-0",
            "padding_bottom_desktop": "desktop:pb-lg",
            "max_width_desktop": "135ch",
            "richtext": "<p>Understanding available options helps make an informed decision. HVAC furnace filters rated MERV 11 to 13 capture dust, pollen, and some finer particles. However, they only work when heating or cooling systems run, leaving gaps in protection. </p><p>Portable air purifiers with advanced filtration provide continuous, targeted filtration in specific rooms. Whole-house systems integrate with existing HVAC infrastructure for comprehensive coverage but require professional installation.</p><p>For most households,<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/collections/air-purifiers\"> <span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">portable air purifiers</span></a> offer the best balance of effectiveness, convenience, and control.</p><h3><strong>Features to Prioritize for Home Health and Comfort</strong></h3><p>When selecting the best air filter for home health, prioritize room size coverage by<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/blogs/news/the-complete-guide-to-selecting-an-air-purifier-based-on-room-size\"> <span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">matching the purifier's capacity to your space</span></a>. Look for noise levels under 30 decibels for bedroom use. Many Blueair models operate as quietly as 18-23 dB on their lowest settings. Smart filter replacement indicators prevent performance drops. </p><p>Energy-efficient designs allow continuous use without excessive electricity consumption. App control and air quality monitoring add convenience. Third-party certifications like AHAM Verifide confirm that performance claims have been independently tested.</p><p>Blueair air purifiers combine powerful performance with thoughtful design, delivering clean air without compromising home aesthetics.</p><h3><strong>FAQs</strong></h3><h4><strong>What is the best air filter for home use?</strong></h4><p>The best air filter combines high particle capture rates with adequate<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/blogs/news/cadr\"> <span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">CADR for your room size</span></a>. Look for units using advanced filtration technology that captures 99.97 percent of particles down to 0.1 microns while operating quietly and efficiently.</p><h4><strong>What is the best air filter for allergies?</strong></h4><p>Air purifiers with true HEPA or HEPASilent™ filtration excel at removing allergy triggers like pollen, dust mites, and<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/blogs/news/air-purifiers-dust-allergies\"> <span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">pet dander</span></a>. Models with activated carbon also eliminate odors and volatile organic compounds that may worsen symptoms.</p><h4><strong>What is the best air filter for asthma?</strong></h4><p><a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/blogs/news/asthma\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">Asthma sufferers</span></a> benefit from purifiers that remove ultrafine particles and run continuously. Choose a unit with automatic sensors that adjust to changing air quality, ensuring consistent protection without manual monitoring.</p><h4><strong>How often should I replace my air filter?</strong></h4><p>Most<a href=\"https://www.blueair.com/collections/air-purifier-filters\"> <span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">air purifier filters</span></a> require replacement every 6 to 9 months, depending on usage and air quality. Models with RealTrack technology monitor filter life based on actual pollutant levels and usage patterns, providing more accurate replacement timing than standard time-based indicators.</p><p>Clean air supports better health, deeper sleep, and improved daily comfort. With the right air filter working in your home, every breath becomes a step toward better well-being.</p>",
            "richtext_alignment": "text-left",
            "richtext_style": "p2"
          }
        }
      },
